  "known_limitations": [
    "Trained on US groundwater (USGS) re-weighted toward Saudi chemistry and passed through an RO simulator - no real Saudi reject samples yet. Next step: fine-tune on pilot-plant samples.",
    "Mode A (sensors only) cannot determine individual ions from conductivity alone; it is a screening mode. Mode B (with last feed lab) is the mode that meets +/-15%.",
    "Simulated 'last lab' staleness is 0-15% random drift; real feed changes (new wells, seasons) may be larger.",
    "Acid dosing is simulated for 60% of brackish plants (H2SO4 to pH 6.5-7.2); antiscalant chemistry is represented only through the limits in assumptions.yaml.",
    "LSI (Langelier) is only valid below 10,000 mg/L TDS; for seawater concentrate it is indicative only (Stiff-Davis would be more appropriate).",
    "Gypsum saturation uses Davies activities with a PHREEQC (phreeqc.dat) calibration; phreeqc.dat is itself approximate above ionic strength ~1 (seawater concentrate); Pitzer would be more accurate.",
    "P10-P90 bands are conformally calibrated on held-out US states; for seawater the Mg band under-covers (no seawater calibration group available).",
    "Conductivity beyond the fitted range (TDS > ~8,700 mg/L) is extrapolated with the FAO slope.",
    "Mg recovery economics use literature price/cost ranges and an assumed small-scale multiplier; no reagent-price sensitivity or site CAPEX is included.",
    "Reuse considers FAO TDS and SAR classes for surface irrigation only (no boron, chloride toxicity, crop tolerance or SAR x ECw infiltration interaction)."
  ],
